%I A399612 #27 Oct 15 2026 09:38:21
%S A399612 2,3,5,7,41,37,31,29,521,509,331,103,101,97,181,173,43,47,83,89,179,
%T A399612 641,631,211,197,191,193,1429,1409,1091,937,941,107,109,337,499,487,
%U A399612 307,293,113,349,347,2953,2917,2879,443,353,359,953,947,2999,2971,2957,709
%N A399612 Labels of successive landing squares of a rook on the Ulam spiral, starting at 2 and repeatedly moving to the smallest prime reachable without revisiting or passing over an earlier landing square.
%C A399612 Use the infinite square lattice with the standard counterclockwise spiral: with 1 at the origin, 2 immediately to its right, and 3 above 2. The rook starts on square 2. At each move it chooses the smallest prime label among all unvisited squares reachable horizontally or vertically without passing through a previously visited square.
%C A399612 Only the starting square and the landing squares are marked as visited. Intermediate squares crossed during a move remain unvisited, including squares bearing primes. Thus an unvisited prime does not obstruct a farther prime in the same direction. Previously traversed segments may be crossed again, provided no previously visited landing square is crossed.
%C A399612 Starting instead at square 1 gives exactly 1 followed by this sequence. The first move is then 1 -> 2, and marking square 1 as visited does not change any subsequent choice: no subsequent move passes through square 1.
%C A399612 The difference from the sequence displayed in A336447 is that here all reachable prime squares are candidates, rather than only the first prime encountered in each direction. For example, from 509 the rook can reach 331 by passing over the still unvisited square 337; the next displayed term of A336447 is instead 337. After prepending 1 to this sequence, the first disagreement with A336447 is at index 12. This distinction is not explicit in the current verbal description of A336447.
%C A399612 The sequence is finite. It contains 69 terms; the last term is a(69) = 503. The terminal position is blocked to the north by the previously visited square 499, to the east by 211, and to the west by 1181. Before these blockers the reachable labels are, respectively, 502,501,500; 418,341,272; and 596,697,806,923,1048. All are composite. The southward ray has no visited blocker, but contains only composite labels: first 504,505,506, and then, at coordinates (-11,-t) for t >= 11, the labels are 4*t^2 + 3*t - 10 = (t+2)*(4*t-5).
%H A399612 Bartlomiej Pawlik, <a href="/A399612/b399612.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..69</a>
%e A399612 a(5) = 41: from 7, the least reachable prime is 41.
%e A399612 a(11) = 331: from a(10) = 509, prime 337 at is crossed on the way to prime 331.
%t A399612 Module[{xy, p = Prime /@ Range[PrimePi[3000]], a = {2}, s = {{1, 0}}, z, q}, xy[n_] := Module[{r = Ceiling[(Sqrt[n] - 1)/2], d}, d = (2 r + 1)^2 - n; Which[d < 2 r, {r - d, -r}, d < 4 r, {-r, -r + d - 2 r}, d < 6 r, {-r + d - 4 r, r}, True, {r, r - d + 6 r}]]; While[True, z = Last[s]; q = SelectFirst[Complement[p, a], Function[k, With[{v = xy[k]}, (v[[1]] == z[[1]] || v[[2]] == z[[2]]) && AllTrue[Most[s], Function[w, Det[{v - z, w - z}] != 0 || (w - z).(v - z) <= 0 || (w - z).(v - z) > (v - z).(v - z)]]]], 0]; If[q == 0, Break[]]; AppendTo[a, q]; AppendTo[s, xy[q]]]; a]
%Y A399612 Cf. A336447, A336413, A336446.
%K A399612 nonn,fini,full,walk
%O A399612 1,1
%A A399612 _Bartlomiej Pawlik_, Oct 10 2026
